  <!-- R61.68 VISIBLE QA: primary controls are sized/readable, table overlays never cover content, and all persistent chrome is recoverable. -->
  <!-- R61.67 DESKTOP SIMPLICITY: flat conventional controls, plain-text secondary actions, no decorative rails/glyph controls, and actual-width responsive layout. -->
  <!-- R61.67 TABLE WORKBENCH: TABLE is a dedicated lightweight grid path with spreadsheet semantics, absolute queue slots and desktop-scale selection behavior. -->
  <!-- R61.67 OPERATIONAL EXCELLENCE: Queue is a purpose-built resizable workstation at ordinary and maximized sizes, with a dedicated transport dock, spreadsheet-like TABLE rows, change-driven rendering and useful space as the default. -->
  <!-- R61.63 PLACE MEMORY / INTERACTION CONTINUITY: R61.61 exact Queue selection/focus, Settings location and authoring-surface continuity remain retained beneath the workstation redesign. -->
  <!-- R61.59 OBS REALITY / ADAPTIVE INSTRUMENTATION / STATE HYGIENE: truthful browser-client/media-path diagnostics, responsive full-player geometry, unified transient-surface policy and removal of retired media-presentation state. -->
  <!-- R61.58 SURFACE COHERENCE / OBS ROUTE CLOSURE / UPDATE LANE: dedicated Mini/Micro appliances, stable chrome, direct thumbnail/video modules, absent disabled media, toggle Inspector, root-first OBS repair and persistent verified update packages. -->
  <!-- R61.57 SEMANTIC TOPOGRAPHY / CONTINUITY MEMORY: queue overview strata, exact workspace-place restoration, navigable Settings cartography, fuzzy intent ranking and visibility-aware controller cadence deepen the operating environment without playback changes or ambient rendering. -->
  <!-- R61.56 RELATIONAL CARTOGRAPHY / CONTEXT MEMORY: clickable queue overview mapping, scroll-aware Settings section location, contextual command-lens state and persistent per-workspace working context turn the scientific console into a spatially coherent operating environment without continuous rendering or playback changes. -->
  <!-- R61.55 COGNITIVE CARTOGRAPHY / OPERATOR GRAMMAR: semantic queue bearings, truthful off-screen NOW locators, contextual Settings indexing, workspace-specific optics and stronger command/focus topology deepen the scientific-console language without continuous rendering or playback changes. -->
  <!-- R61.54 PHASE LATTICE / INFORMATION OPTICS: sparse phase contours, edge scales and semantic apertures deepen the scientific-console hierarchy while preserving R61.53 state choreography, low-cost rendering and zero layout motion. -->
  <!-- R61.53 VECTOR DATUM / INTERACTION CHOREOGRAPHY: mode-aware optical fields, workspace registration corners, one-shot state impulses, transport symmetry and a live queue horizon marker deepen the scientific-instrument language without continuous animation or playback changes. -->
  <!-- R61.52 SIGNAL TOPOLOGY: large registration landmarks, semantic state rails, calibration focus reticles and deeper optical field hierarchy. Interaction remains stable and low-cost; playback authority is untouched. -->
  <!-- R61.51 DATUM INSTRUMENT: authored scientific-computing art direction. Sparse calibration texture, geometric state marks and instrument framing deepen character without adding feature chrome or touching playback authority. -->
  <!-- R61.49 MICRO APPLIANCE: first scale-ladder surface, independent Micro geometry, shared playback authority, and stable zero-reflow transport feedback. -->
  <!-- R61.48 GEOMETRY CONTRACT: 1280x720 usability floor, 1600x900 preferred workspace, human-size targets, scroll-safe tool surfaces, and zero hover reflow. -->
  <!-- R61.47.1 WPF Runtime Gate Closure: runtime-XAML repair + installer load probe; presentation remains Instrument Surface III. -->
  <!-- R61.47 Instrument Surface III: seamless precision-instrument hierarchy. Remove unnecessary card boundaries, tighten the workbench rhythm, and let state emerge through hairlines, motion and contrast rather than UI furniture. -->
  <!-- R61.46 Instrument Surface II: premium creative-instrument visual hierarchy, tactile micro-geometry and subconscious optical depth without ornamental chrome. -->
  <!-- R61.40 Authority Honesty + Native Reports: Performance exposes only engine-backed controls; reports stay inside YOMI as selectable/copyable text instead of opening external .txt documents. -->
  <!-- R61.37 Calm Defaults + Exception Surfacing: Broadcast stays player-first, healthy telemetry stays quiet, and only real attention states interrupt the normal surface. -->
  <!-- R61.41 Playlist Pool 2: reusable named Pool definitions and balanced-source mixing while preserving the default true global shuffle. -->
  <!-- R61.36 Progressive Disclosure + Native Text: keep the OBS fast path genuinely first, move broadcast engineering behind deliberate expansion, keep playlist editing inside YOMI, and remove another redundant player telemetry line while preserving R61.35 crop/Mini/OBS continuity. -->
  <!-- R61.34 Queue Authority Closure: authoritative engine receipts, real block/checkpoint handlers, atomic batch order mutations, and a commit barrier over the R61.33 fidelity layer. -->
  <!-- R61 Window State Fidelity: normal bounds, maximized intent, tray restore and queue drawer geometry are monitor-aware and reversible. -->
  <!-- R60 Cohesion Fidelity: first visible frame is hydrated, startup stays compact, direct-state feedback stays quiet, and ordinary chrome never outranks playback reality. -->
  <!-- R56 Shell Fidelity: native-looking custom chrome is compact, fully themed, resize-stable, and guarantees primary transport visibility; controller video preparation is restored. -->
  <!-- R55 Visual Rhythm Fidelity: shared control metrics, theme-coherent neutrals, integer typography and optical alignment; no added chrome. -->
  <!-- R49 Orientation Fidelity: first-hour comprehension is layered into existing status, queue, media and Help surfaces without tutorial chrome. -->
  <!-- R48 Context Continuity: existing surfaces preserve placement, working focus, runtime ownership, and recovered geometry without new chrome. -->
  <!-- R47 Interaction Fidelity: existing surfaces preserve drafts, focus, geometry, and no-op semantics without new chrome. -->
